---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: device-runtime
covers: subtree
purpose: Device-private executable custody and ephemeral session identity, independent of transport.
rules:
  - id: rust-style-strict
    policy: rust-style-strict@1
---

The release record and session pins are private device records (B); the status view is
reconstructed (C). No new DHT entries, coordinator calls, signals or recurring network heads.
Binary identity uses eprfs-core raw CIDs; release manifests use its canonical DAG-CBOR codec.
Ingest verifies bytes; land alone advances current after provenance, ancestry and health.
The launcher trusts ingested immutable files, as the preceding Python exec path did.
Private local custody has no public reach claim. Cross-device custody belongs to slice B.
